## 1. Purpose

This report shows whether the MedHarness installed here stops what it is relied on to stop, in this environment. `medharness build validation` ran each case of the validation set that ships with the release against a scratch project in a temporary directory, through the same command line a user runs. It did not read any project's DHF, and `--dhf` was ignored. It did not reach the network.

The report is evidence for the user's validation of MedHarness for their intended use (ISO 13485 §4.1.6). The assessment of any deviation below, the decision that the tool is fit for that use, and the signature are the user's.

